    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-act-2006-sch-2-sec-95aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95AA Guidelines for National Privacy Principles about genetic",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-act-2006#sch-2-sec-95aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "information\nOverview\n\n(1) This section allows the Commissioner to approve for the purposes\nof the National Privacy Principles (the NPPs) guidelines that are\nissued by the National Health and Medical Research Council.\n\nAmendments relating to genetic information  Schedule 2\n\nApproving guidelines for use and disclosure\n\n(2) For the purposes of subparagraph 2.1(ea)(ii) of the NPPs, the\nCommissioner may, by legislative instrument, approve guidelines\nthat relate to the use and disclosure of genetic information for the\npurposes of lessening or preventing a serious threat to the life,\nhealth or safety (whether or not the threat is imminent) of an\nindividual who is a genetic relative of the individual to whom the\ngenetic information relates.\nReview by AAT\n\n(3) Application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal\nfor review of a decision of the Commissioner to refuse to approve\nguidelines.",
      "skos:definition": "information\nOverview\n\n(1) This section allows the Commissioner to approve for the purposes\nof the National Privacy Principles (the NPPs) guidelines that are\nissued by the National Health and Medical Research Council.\n\nAmendments relating to genetic information  Schedule 2\n\nApproving guidelines for use and disclosure\n\n(2) For the purposes of subparagraph 2.1(ea)(ii) of the NPPs, the\nCommissioner may, by legislative instrument, approve guidelines\nthat relate to the use and disclosure of genetic information for the\npurposes of lessening or preventing a serious threat to the life,\nhealth or safety (whether or not the threat is imminent) of an\nindividual who is a genetic relative of the individual to whom the\ngenetic information relates.\nReview by AAT\n\n(3) Application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal\nfor review of a decision of the Commissioner to refuse to approve\nguidelines.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-act-2006-sch-2-sec-95aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-act-2006-sch-2-sec-95aa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-act-2006-sch-2-sec-95aa-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "094eb9cf0ac16e0b2f3a2ee28b9483827159ee873494ea8c8814a69a13d5bbb6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-act-2006#sch-2-sec-95aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95AA Guidelines for National Privacy Principles about genetic",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "information\nOverview\n\n(1) This section allows the Commissioner to approve for the purposes\nof the National Privacy Principles (the NPPs) guidelines that are\nissued by the National Health and Medical Research Council.\n\nAmendments relating to genetic information  Schedule 2\n\nApproving guidelines for use and disclosure\n\n(2) For the purposes of subparagraph 2.1(ea)(ii) of the NPPs, the\nCommissioner may, by legislative instrument, approve guidelines\nthat relate to the use and disclosure of genetic information for the\npurposes of lessening or preventing a serious threat to the life,\nhealth or safety (whether or not the threat is imminent) of an\nindividual who is a genetic relative of the individual to whom the\ngenetic information relates.\nReview by AAT\n\n(3) Application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal\nfor review of a decision of the Commissioner to refuse to approve\nguidelines."
    },
    {
